      ],
      "finalAnswer": 2,
      "explanation": [
        "The cross-coupled NOR latch uses exactly 2 NOR gates. When S=1 and R=0, Q sets to 1. When S=0 and R=1, Q resets to 0. When S=0 and R=0, the feedback loop latches the previous state."
      ],
      "learningObjective": "Analyze bistable feedback loops in basic cross-coupled NOR latch memory elements.",
